A good shape here is “library + example apps” in a Turborepo/Nx-style layout: /apps for RN/example apps and /packages for the core melon stack. This matches common monorepo guidance and how people organize Prisma and shared libraries today.

Below is a concrete structure and package boundaries that line up with the PRDs you’ve drafted.

Top-level layout
text
melon-monorepo/
  apps/
    playground-rn/        # Example RN app using new arch + melon/db
    playground-web/       # Optional web example (if/when supported)
    docs/                 # Docusaurus/Next docs site for the lib
  packages/
    melon-db/             # @melon/db core (schema, AST, engine)
    melon-db-sqlite/      # @melon/db-sqlite RN/Node SQLite adapter
    melon-db-react/       # @melon/db-react (hooks, provider)
    melon-db-query/       # @melon/db-query fluent builder
    melon-db-query-mango/ # @melon/db-query-mango Mango -> AST
    melon-db-prisma/      # @melon/db-prisma schema import + client
    melon-db-devtools/    # @melon/db-devtools devtools bridge/UI
    melon-db-testkit/     # @melon/db-testkit in-memory, helpers
    melon-db-codemods/    # @melon/db-codemods migration helpers
    melon-sync/           # @melon/sync core (separate PRD)
    melon-sync-server/    # @melon/sync-server backend helpers
  tooling/
    tsconfig.base.json
    eslint.config.mjs
    jest.config.base.ts
    turbo.json            # or nx.json, etc.
  package.json
  pnpm-workspace.yaml     # or yarn/pnpm workspaces
  README.md
This mirrors common monorepo practice where /apps consume /packages and shared DB/ORM logic sits in a packages/* folder.

Package boundaries
packages/melon-db – core engine
Name: @melon/db
Role: Single source of truth for schema, AST, adapter contract, transactions, and subscriptions. No React, no Prisma, no Mango here.

Depends on:

No other melon-* packages (bottom of the stack)

Only generic deps (TypeScript, zod/valibot if you want runtime validation)

Key exports (from the TS interfaces doc):

MelonSchema, CollectionMetadata, DatabaseSchemaDefinition

QueryAst, QueryPlan, PreparedQuery

StorageAdapter, AdapterWriteOperation, AdapterChangeSet

MelonDatabase, MelonCollection, MelonQueryHandle

Factories: createDatabase, createQueryFactory

WatermelonDB’s Database + DatabaseAdapter + Collection live conceptually here, but with more explicit typing and AST.

packages/melon-db-sqlite – SQLite adapter
Name: @melon/db-sqlite
Role: Production adapter for RN new architecture (JSI/TurboModule) and possibly Node.

Depends on:

@melon/db (for StorageAdapter and AST)

Native libs (react-native-sqlite/JSI, etc.)

Key exports:

createSqliteAdapter(options): StorageAdapter

This is the concrete version of what WatermelonDB currently does with its SQLite adapter, but as a clean package that only knows about the AST and adapter interface.

packages/melon-db-query – fluent query builder
Name: @melon/db-query
Role: First-party fluent query builder that outputs QueryAst.

Depends on:

@melon/db for AST types

Key exports:

QueryBuilder, QueryFactory

createQueryFactory(schema: MelonSchema): QueryFactory

This is your “canonical” type-safe builder, designed for pure functions and reuse.

packages/melon-db-query-mango – Mango DSL
Name: @melon/db-query-mango
Role: Parse and validate Mango-style selectors and compile them into QueryAst.

Depends on:

@melon/db (AST)

Maybe small parsing/validation utilities

Key exports:

MangoQuery, MangoSelector

createMangoCompiler(): MangoQueryCompiler

The implementation follows RxDB/CouchDB-style Mango semantics for selector, sort, limit, etc., translating into your AST.

packages/melon-db-react – React bindings
Name: @melon/db-react
Role: Hooks and providers around MelonDatabase and PreparedQuery.

Depends on:

@melon/db for runtime types

Optionally @melon/db-query / @melon/db-query-mango for helper overloads

Key exports:

<MelonDbProvider db={...}>

useDatabase, useCollection

useQuery(ast | prepared), useFindMany, useMangoQuery

useWriter (wraps db.write)

Matches the “observable local DB + React hooks” pattern that both WatermelonDB and Prisma’s RN support are converging on.

packages/melon-db-prisma – Prisma integration
Name: @melon/db-prisma
Role: Prisma-style schema import and generated local client facades.

Depends on:

@melon/db (schema + AST)

Optionally @melon/db-query for building AST under the hood

@prisma/sdk or parser as a dev dependency for schema parsing

Key exports:

PrismaSchemaImporter, PrismaCodeGenerator

createPrismaLikeClient(db: MelonDatabase): PrismaLikeClient

This is “Prisma-like on top of melon,” not “melon running Prisma engine,” which matches Prisma’s messaging of early RN/Expo support and keeps @melon/db in control of local execution.

packages/melon-db-devtools – devtools bridge
Name: @melon/db-devtools
Role: Debugging bridge and optional UI.

Depends on:

@melon/db (AST, adapter operations)

Possibly @melon/db-react for React devtools UI

Key exports:

DevtoolsBridge

<MelonDevtoolsPanel /> or integration for React Native/Web devtools

AST + SQL inspector is especially helpful when juggling multiple query surfaces.

packages/melon-db-testkit – test utilities
Name: @melon/db-testkit
Role: Testing helpers and in-memory adapters.

Depends on:

@melon/db (adapter, AST)

Optionally @melon/db-query for fluent test queries

Key exports:

createInMemoryAdapter()

Factories for ephemeral databases

Jest helpers (e.g. withTestDatabase)

WatermelonDB users have had to build a lot of this themselves; here it’s packaged.

packages/melon-db-codemods – migration helpers
Name: @melon/db-codemods
Role: Migration tooling for existing WatermelonDB apps.

Depends on:

TS AST tooling (ts-morph, jscodeshift)

@melon/db types for mapping

Key exports:

CLI codemods for database.get('table').query(...) → db.collection('table').query(...)

Mappers for Watermelon query descriptors → AST

WatermelonDB’s clear separation of Database/Collection/Adapter is what makes this feasible.

packages/melon-sync and packages/melon-sync-server
These follow from your earlier PRD, but at a high level:

@melon/sync depends only on @melon/db and its change APIs.

@melon/sync-server depends on Node adapter libraries and exports backend helpers.

They do not depend on the query-layer packages (query, mango, prisma) so that sync remains orthogonal.

Apps and how they depend on packages
apps/playground-rn
Uses: @melon/db, @melon/db-sqlite, @melon/db-react, @melon/db-query (and optionally @melon/sync).

Purpose: RN New Architecture demo, perf harness, example app.

This is where you validate the RN-specific setup guidance that WatermelonDB currently documents separately.

apps/playground-web
Uses: @melon/db plus a future web adapter package if/when needed.

Purpose: Optional for showing web compatibility.

apps/docs
Uses: @melon/db, @melon/db-react, @melon-db-query-*, @melon-db-prisma as dependencies for live code blocks.

Purpose: Documentation site.

Tooling layout
A simple, conventional choice:

text
melon-monorepo/
  turbo.json              # or nx.json
  package.json
  pnpm-workspace.yaml     # all packages/* and apps/* as workspaces
  tsconfig.base.json      # base TS config extended by packages/apps
  eslint.config.mjs
  jest.config.base.ts
Then each package has:

text
packages/melon-db/
  src/
    index.ts
    schema.ts
    ast.ts
    adapter.ts
    database.ts
  package.json
  tsconfig.json
  jest.config.ts
  README.md
This is similar to how people place Prisma-based database packages inside packages/database in a Turborepo, then consume them from apps.

Dependency rules summary
To keep things clean and tree-shakeable:

@melon/db – core; must not import any other melon-*.

@melon/db-sqlite, @melon-db-query, @melon-db-query-mango, @melon-db-prisma, @melon-db-testkit – can depend on @melon/db but not on each other (unless clearly a higher-level layer).

@melon/db-react, @melon/db-devtools – higher-level; can depend on @melon/db and query packages, but not on sync.

@melon/sync – depends on @melon/db only.

apps/* – can depend on any packages.